# zip and try_zip. Plain `zip` keeps the shorter list's length; `try_zip` puts a row whose lists
# differ in length in lane 1 as `()`, and zips the others in lane 0. Here element e gives lhs [0..e)
# and rhs [0..e+(e&1)) — so even e zips (lane 0) and odd e mismatches (lane 1).
# n = 4
# = List ends=[4] <(List ends=[0, 1, 3, 6] <([0, 0, 1, 0, 1, 2], [0, 0, 1, 0, 1, 2])>, Sum tags=[0, 1, 0, 1] [List ends=[0, 2] <([0, 1], [0, 1])>, ()x2])>
input iota map (x -> let pair = (x iota, (x, x and 1) add iota) in (pair zip, pair try_zip))
